From bb7df52c89496367f9cb4fc197e553086e102185 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:57:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ProgressBar: only run the indeterminate animation while it is
 shown

The indeterminate stripes' NumberAnimation runs with running: true and
infinite loops, so every ProgressBar animates its hidden indeterminate
fill for as long as it exists, even in determinate mode or while the bar
is invisible. A running animation keeps the window rendering at the
display's refresh rate.

Plasma Mobile's notification cards contain a determinate ProgressBar, so
a lock screen showing a notification redraws continuously: on an MT8173
tablet kscreenlocker_greet used ~75% of a CPU and presented ~60 frames/s
with nothing changing on screen.

Run the animation only while the indeterminate fill is visible, which is
already bound to the indeterminate state and follows the control's
effective visibility.
---
 style/qtquickcontrols/ProgressBar.qml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/style/qtquickcontrols/ProgressBar.qml b/style/qtquickcontrols/ProgressBar.qml
index 097da8d..a7e3d09 100644
--- a/style/qtquickcontrols/ProgressBar.qml
+++ b/style/qtquickcontrols/ProgressBar.qml
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ T.ProgressBar {
                 to: 0
                 duration: 3 * Kirigami.Units.veryLongDuration
                 loops: Animation.Infinite
-                running: true
+                running: indeterminateFill.visible
             }
         }
     }
